@startuml

title Disconnection and reconnection

participant Client1
participant Server
participant Client2

loop every 2 seconds while connected
Client1->Server: HeartbeatRequest(game, nickname)
Server-->Client1: GameOperationResult.SimpleOk(I am active)
end

Client1 -x Server: connection or heartbeat stops
Server->Server: heartbeat expires after 8 seconds
Server->Server: mark player disconnected and remove subscriber
Server-->Client2: GameViewUpdate(player disconnected)

alt at least two players remain connected
opt disconnected player owns the active turn
Server->Server: skip disconnected player's turn
Server-->Client2: GameViewUpdate(turn skipped)
end
else only one player remains connected
Server-->Client2: GameViewUpdate(game suspended)
alt player reconnects within 60 seconds
Client1->Server: NicknameRequest
Server-->Client1: GameOperationResult.Nickname(rejoinAvailable = true)
Client1->Server: JoinGameRequest(rejoin = true)
Server-->Client2: GameViewUpdate(player reconnected)
Server-->Client1: GameOperationResult.Snapshot(Player reconnected, snapshot)
Client1->Server: SubscribeGameRequest
Server-->Client1: GameOperationResult.Snapshot(current snapshot)
else 60-second timeout expires
Server->Server: declare the only connected player winner
Server-->Client2: GameViewUpdate(finished snapshot)
end
end

note over Client1, Client2
Rejoining restores the game session, but the client must
subscribe again because the old update sink was removed.
end note

@enduml
